Unreleased
----------

- Adds `get_ability(user)`: builds the rules of a user only once per request, `clear_abilities()` resets it
- `can`/`ensure` stop at the first matching rule instead of evaluating every condition
- Fixes monitored flask-classy views on blueprints not being checked
- Fixes `ensure_authorization` answering 500 instead of 403 (and 404 for unknown urls) outside debug mode
- Fixes a globally registered `bouncer.authorization_method` being merged into the app's rules
- Fixes `Bouncer.get_app()` without a bound app
- `ensure` no longer puts the user and subject into the 403 description (it is sent to the client), they are logged at debug level
- Conditional `can` rules no longer allow a class: `can(EDIT, Article)` was true as soon as any conditional EDIT rule
  existed. Conditional `cannot` rules still forbid it. This also applies to the implicit checks of monitored
  flask-classy views, which test the `__target_model__` class

Version 0.3.0
-------------

- Adds `can` method
- Drops Python 2.7 support
- Adds Python 3.8 support

Version 0.2.0
-------------

- Raises Forbidden (403) instead of Unauthorized (401)
- Drops Python 2.6 support

Version 0.1.13
--------------

- Adds init_app method
- More standard way of registering extensions
- Added AUTHORS file
- Added CHANGES file